ef exactly \"https://myvm.exe.xyz:8000/preview\", target \"_blank\" and rel \"noopener noreferrer\", and background-color \"rgb(240, 240, 240)\". e. Hover the link; its color should be \"rgb(128, 0, 0)\". f. Use the keyboard: eval window.statusItem('branch').focus(), press Tab, then press Shift+Tab as a key_down step \"Shift\", a press_key step \"Tab\" and a key_up step \"Shift\". g. Eval window.statusFocusRing('branch'), window.statusFocusRing('model') and window.statusFocusRing('link'), each with expect \"ok\". h. Hover the picker (\".model-picker-inline\" in the row); its color should be \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\". i. Click the picker. \".model-picker-panel\" should be visible and have at least one \".p-select-option\". Click the button named exactly \"Close\" in \".model-picker-panel\"; the panel should become hidden; the picker's color should be \"rgb(0, 0, 0)\". j. Call \"mark diffs\", then click the button named \"Review commit\" in the row. Call \"diff requested\" with expect \"true\". \".diff-viewer-overlay\" should be visible; click its \".diff-viewer-close\"; the overlay should become hidden. k. Click the branch. \".git-graph-container\" should be visible; click the button named exactly \"Close\" in it; it should become hidden. l. Only when W is 390: eval window.statusRowScrolls() with expect \"ok\". 2. For each N of 1 then 2, with the error E being \"commmit\" for 1 and \"full or abbreviated commit hash\" for 2: a. Call \"bad commit N\" (the hook now prints one \"Bad commit\" item with bad arguments), then reload the page. b. The row's text should be exactly \"Status hook failed\", and \".diff-viewer-overlay\" count 0. c. Click the button named \"Status hook failed\" in the row. d. The dialog named \"Status hook error\" ([role=\"dialog\"][aria-label=\"Status hook error\"]) should contain E and be entirely within the viewport. e. Press Escape; the dialog should become hidden; the row's text should still be exactly \"Status hook failed\".",
